  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set covering both sides of the contract:\n\n**FastAPI request validation chain:**\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` \u2014 `request_body_to_args`, `get_body_field`, core body parsing/validation dispatch\n- `fastapi/_compat.py` \u2014 Pydantic v1/v2 compatibility shims (`is_scalar_field`, model validation calls)\n- `fastapi/routing.py` \u2014 route handler wiring that invokes dependency resolution and body validation\n- `fastapi/encoders.py` \u2014 `jsonable_encoder`, used both for response serialization and comparable to what a client should produce\n- `fastapi/exceptions.py` / `fastapi/exception_handlers.py` \u2014 `RequestValidationError` and the 422 handler\n- `fastapi/params.py` \u2014 `Body`, `Query`, etc. parameter/field metadata\n- `fastapi/applications.py` \u2014 app-level wiring of exception handlers and OpenAPI content-type negotiation\n\n**httpx request encoding chain:**\n- `httpx/_content.py` \u2014 `encode_json`, `encode_request`, Content-Type header assignment\n- `httpx/_models.py` \u2014 `Request`/`Response` construction, header handling\n- `httpx/_client.py` \u2014 top-level `post`/`request` methods that route `json=` kwarg into encoding\n- `httpx/_types.py` \u2014 type aliases governing what shapes are accepted for `json=`\n- `httpx/_multipart.py` \u2014 alternate encoding path for comparison (form/multipart vs JSON)",
